Z||000000||MrFeeArrow||01-29-2000||10:53 AM||||Any good info on the Quad Four engine swap. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||pherder||01-29-2000||11:09 AM||||I am about to complete my second Quad 4 into a Fiero swap.<P>My personal feelings are that it is almost as hard a swap as any non-Fiero engine swap out there.<P>One, you have to combind the wiring harnass from the Quad 4 to the Fiero's.<P>Two, you have to either use a kit or have the engine/trans mounts built.<P>Three, the transaxle used MUST be from the Quad 4 engine (only one that will bolt to it!)<P>Four, if it is a 5 speed (Getrag), you will need Rodney Dickman's FWD Getrag to Fiero adapter kit to make you shifting work.<P>Be advised, the newer Getrags DO NOT have the mounting bosses needed for the Fiero's Getrag mounts or shift cables.  You will have to make something work.<P>Plumbing of coolant and A/C will take some work.  I have $100 in a modified Fiero A/C hose just to shorten it and put in a High Pressure sensor in the line.  Depending on the model of Fiero (i.e. 84-86 have two heater hoses ... 87-88 have one, the other is already plumbed into the coolant tube at the right rear) and this needs to be addressed when installing the coolant lines.<P>Fuel hoses need to be run and if you have a L4 now, you will have to replace the fuel pump with a V6 version.<P>If you have an 87-88 L4, the throttle cable is correct, if you have anything else, you will have to modify or change out to the 87-88 L4 cable.<P>The list goes on.<P>But hey!  I'm one for sell abuse ... <P>88 Coupe - HO Quad4 w/Isuzu 5 speed (current project)<BR>88 Formula - Chevy V8 w/TPI (third project)<BR>88 GT - 3.1 to be installed (second project)<P>3 Fieros (one of each model produced in 1988!) None of them with an engine installed  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Project page @  <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=208525" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=208525</A> <P>Paul||||reg||4
Z||000002||MrFeeArrow||01-29-2000||11:34 AM||||Thanks Pherder.<BR>Are there any kits available?||||reg||12
